\lispPackageChapter{livermore/threshold}

The \texttt{livermore/threshold} package is a single generic used as a
target function for XCSR: whether a point meets or exceeds a threshold.

\lispGenericSubsection{threshold-indicator}

True if \lispVar{instance} meets or exceeds \lispVar{threshold}.

A number meets a number when $\mathit{instance} \ge \mathit{threshold}$.  A
list or vector meets another of the same length when every coordinate
satisfies that comparison.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(threshold-indicator \lispVar{threshold} \lispVar{instance})}

\lispExamples

\begin{lstlisting}
(threshold-indicator 5 6)           ; => T
(threshold-indicator '(1 2) '(2 2)) ; => T
(threshold-indicator #(1 2) #(2 1)) ; => NIL
\end{lstlisting}
